---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CounterIllustration from "../../components/CounterIllustration.astro";
import PNCounterDemo from "../../components/PNCounterDemo.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import { pnCounterTerm } from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="PN-counter"
  description="Bob corrects a duplicate bird sighting while Alice records new birds. A PN-counter preserves both concurrent updates."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="PN-counter"
>
  <article class="structure-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structures</p>
      <h1>PN-counter</h1>
      <p class="structure-summary">
        Alice, Bob, and Carol have agreed on 10 birds. Then Bob finds a
        duplicate sighting while Alice counts 3 new birds on another trail.
        Their shared counter must preserve the new sightings and the
        correction.
      </p>
    </header>

    <StructureFacts
      family="CRDT"
      model="State-based convergent replicated data type"
      updates="Increment and decrement"
      merge="Merge positive and negative per-replica counts by maximum, then subtract."
      delivery="Safe under repeated and out-of-order delivery"
      bestFor="Offline or unreliable counters that need corrections"
      cost="Two integers for each replica"
    />
    <CounterIllustration kind="pn-counter" />

    <section aria-labelledby="correction-title">
      <h2 id="correction-title">Bob finds a duplicate sighting</h2>
      <p>
        Bob spots a mistake in the agreed count: one line records the same bird
        twice. His contribution should fall by one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bob cannot lower a G-counter component. An older note with the larger
        value could arrive later and restore the mistake. The merge rule must
        keep the larger value.
      </p>
      <p>
        A{" "}
        <dfn><a href="/glossary/#pn-counter">PN-counter</a></dfn> records the
        correction instead. It keeps one grow-only counter for sightings and a
        second grow-only counter for corrections. Both sides merge by maximum.
        The visible count subtracts one total from the other.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...pnCounterTerm} />
      <pre aria-label="PN-counter bird total rule"><code>birds = sightings - corrections</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="correction-race-title">
      <h2 id="correction-race-title">Two new notes leave at once</h2>
      <p>
        While Bob writes a correction for the duplicate sighting, Alice counts
        3 more birds on the ridge trail. Neither has received the other's note.
        Alice's view rises from 10 to 13. Bob's falls from 10 to 9. Carol still
        reads 10.
      </p>
      <table aria-label="Bird count before PN-counter notes arrive">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Moment</th>
            <th scope="col">Alice</th>
            <th scope="col">Bob</th>
            <th scope="col">Carol</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Agreed count</th><td>10</td><td>10</td><td>10</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Notes waiting</th><td>13</td><td>9</td><td>10</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Both notes arrive</th><td>12</td><td>12</td><td>12</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        The two notes do not cancel in transit. Alice's positive component
        grows by 3, and Bob's correction component grows by 1. Every hiker
        eventually computes <code>13 - 1 = 12</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <PNCounterDemo />

    <section aria-labelledby="result-title">
      <h2 id="result-title">The correction survives the merge</h2>
      <p>
        After both notes arrive, the sightings side totals 13 and the
        corrections side totals 1. Alice, Bob, and Carol all read 12 birds.
        Delivery order does not change that result, and a repeated delta does
        not apply the correction twice.
      </p>
      <p>
        A PN-counter can also produce a negative value. That is correct counter
        behavior, but it may be invalid for the thing being counted. An
        application that must never show fewer than zero birds needs another
        rule to prevent or coordinate those updates.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="notes-title">
      <h2 id="notes-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        This lesson calls Watershed's public{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/pn_counter_kernel.gleam">PN-counter kernel</a>
        {" "}and sends the three hikers' notes through Sluice.
      </p>
      <p>
        The merge rule follows the state-based positive-negative counter
        described in{" "}
        <a href="https://inria.hal.science/inria-00555588/document">A comprehensive study of Convergent and Commutative Replicated Data Types</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through structures">
      <a href="/structures/g-counter/">Back to G-counter</a>
      <a href="/structures/">Browse all structures</a>
      <a href="/atlas/multi-value-registers/">Continue to registers</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .structure-page {
    max-width: var(--measure-reading);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .structure-page > section {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }

  .structure-summary {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .structure-page > section > p dfn {
    color: var(--signal);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .structure-page > section > p dfn a {
    color: inherit;
  }

  pre {
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--clear) 45%, var(--sky-sheet));
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    margin-block: var(--space-5);
    border-collapse: collapse;
  }

  :is(th, td) {
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  th {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
  }

  td {
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .structure-next {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 650;
  }
</style>
